    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green: **58 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed owner deletion to a soft-delete. Here's what I did:\n\n**Model** (`Owner.java`)\n- Added a `deleted` boolean field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\")`) with a `getDeleted()`/`setDeleted()` pair. `getDeleted()` returns non-null (`false` when unset), so a newly created owner is `deleted: false` without any extra initialization.\n\n**API schema** (`openapi.yml`)\n- Added a read-only `deleted` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct maps it automatically. This is what surfaces `$.deleted` on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Database schema** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`)\n- Added a `deleted BOOLEAN` column to the `owners` table. The tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to be declared in `schema.sql` explicitly.\n\n**Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)\n- `deleteOwner` now sets `deleted = true` and calls `saveOwner` (retaining the row) instead of `deleteOwner`, still returning `204 No Content` (2xx).\n- The create endpoint's **household-duplicate**, **identity-key**, and **possible-duplicate** checks now filter out owners flagged `deleted`, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\nThe new `Cp46Tests` (both cases) and all 57 existing tests pass.",
